{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>A grating.</b> A term of כְּבָרָה, which they call קרי\"בלא בְּלַעַז — a kind of garment made for the altar, made with holes, hole after hole, like a net. And this verse is inverted, and this is its resolution: 'And you shall make for it a grating of copper, the work of a net.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "the la'az קרי\"בלא is Old French cribl(e), 'sieve' or 'mesh strainer'; the verse is 'inverted' (מְסֹרָס) because the phrase מַעֲשֵׂה רֶשֶׁת, 'the work of a net,' appears to belong with מִכְבַּר, 'grating,' rather than being read in sequence."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:56.091870303Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}